# Only if your proxy / hosting layer cannot carry WebSockets.
# "Choose whether the n8n backend uses server-sent events (sse) or WebSockets (websocket) to send changes to the UI",
# default websocket (n8n deployment environment variables docs).
# Tested on n8n 2.41.3 (2026-09-30) behind the broken scenario-A nginx config (no Upgrade/Connection headers):
# with this set, the editor connected and the test workflow ran. Reload open editor tabs after the restart.
N8N_PUSH_BACKEND=sse
